' Question: where is a channel registered, and who asks whether one is carried?
' Explained by: ../05-building-blocks.md, which cites each component. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 05-channel-catalog
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction
[CHANNEL_DESCRIPTORS] as CDS
[RegisteredChannelCatalog] as C
[DiscordWebhookChannel] as D
[ChannelAlertingStatus] as CS
[SendTestMessage] as ST
[DescriptorChannelCatalogBuilder] as DB
[SendTestToConfiguredChannels] as OT
[DiscordWebhookSetup] as WS
[operations:\nAlertingAlertChannels] as OA
CDS --> C : build_channel_catalog; a channel\nwith no webhook is left out
C --> D : holds each configured channel
CS --> C : in the catalog and not disabled
OA --> CS : IAlertingStatus\ncarries_bot_events
ST --> C : one TEST alert per channel,\nnever the outbox
OT --> DB : the Options page's Send test asks for a catalog now
DB --> CDS : build_channel_catalog again, a new catalog\nthat the run's one is not replaced by
OT --> ST : one TEST alert per channel of that catalog
WS --> C : running = the run has the Discord lane\n(read only, never changed)
@enduml
